WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.563
Frequency agility moves the radar's carrier to a new channel for every pulse, so a jammer parked on one frequency misses most of them.

2
00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:13.900
A follower jammer listens instead, and jumps to each new channel.

3
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.200
But detecting and retuning takes time, here 4 microseconds.

4
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.261
Until then it is still on the old channel.

5
00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:26.289
With 20 microsecond pulses it still covers 80 percent of every dwell.

6
00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:29.759
Now hop eight times inside each pulse.

7
00:00:29.809 --> 00:00:39.352
Each dwell lasts 2.5 microseconds, shorter than the reaction time, so by the time the jammer lands the radar has already moved.

8
00:00:40.002 --> 00:00:47.355
The jammer's best answer is then to spread its power over all sixteen channels, which is twelve decibels weaker.

9
00:00:47.405 --> 00:00:52.313
The rule is simple: make the dwell shorter than the jammer's reaction time.

10
00:00:52.363 --> 00:00:56.808
A faster jammer still lands, and that limit is stated in the Studio.
